        "text": "The equals method compares the value of two string objects rather than their addresses.",
        "refs": ["Q0001", "Q0002", "Q0003"],
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "Because these operators will compare the address of our string objects, not their value.",
            "basis": "explicit",
            "availability": "SOURCE_SUPPORTED",
            "literal_kind": "verbal",
            "instructional_role": "explanation_of_mistake",
            "refs": ["Q0001"],
            "related_refs": []
          },
          {
            "text": "So if you have two strings, quit and quit, but stored in different memory locations, they have different addresses.",
            "basis": "explicit",
            "availability": "SOURCE_SUPPORTED",
            "literal_kind": "verbal",
            "instructional_role": "explanation_of_mistake",
            "refs": ["Q0002"],
            "related_refs": []
          },
          {
            "text": "So we cannot use the inequality operator to compare their value.",
            "basis": "explicit",
            "availability": "SOURCE_SUPPORTED",
            "literal_kind": "verbal",
            "instructional_role": "identified_mistake",
            "refs": ["Q0003"],
            "related_refs": []
          }
        ]
      },
      "context": null
    },
